# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# There was no .gitattributes here, and 2,131 of 2,132 content files were CRLF.
# That is fine until something derives content from the files: the CI gate
# rebuilds api/prompt-index.json and compares it to the committed copy, and the
# index embeds a 200-character contentPreview verbatim. Built on Windows it
# carried \r\n, rebuilt on a Linux runner it carried \n, so the gate could never
# pass. `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) is what makes the Windows checkout match
# the Linux one, so the index is reproducible on either.

*               text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the types we actually carry, so a stray heuristic cannot flip one.
*.md            text eol=lf
*.MD            text eol=lf
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.ts            text eol=lf
*.tsx           text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.svg           text eol=lf
*.xml           text eol=lf
*.xsd           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.csv           text eol=lf
*.tex           text eol=lf
*.mplstyle      text eol=lf
LICENSE         text eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.ico           binary
*.ttf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.zip           binary
*.pdf           binary
